Problem Statement

To design and implement a Food Order Management System using a Linked List in C++ that helps manage food orders in restaurants and college canteens in an organized and efficient manner. 
The system aims to overcome the difficulties associated with manual order management, such as maintaining order records, searching for orders, deleting cancelled orders, and calculating the total bill. It allows users to add new food orders, display all order details, search for a particular order, delete an existing order, and calculate the total amount of orders. 
The linked list data structure is used to store order information dynamically, allowing nodes to be created and deleted according to requirements. 
This project focuses on implementing fundamental linked list operations such as insertion, deletion, searching, and traversal while understanding the use of pointers and dynamic memory allocation in C++. 
The system provides a basic approach to managing food orders and demonstrates the practical application of data structures in solving real-world problems.

